# Jurnii Design System

Before building or editing UI:

1. Read [docs/website-design-system.md](../../docs/website-design-system.md) first (architecture, components, voice, checklist).
2. Consult [docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md) for token lookups (palettes, semantic chains, themes).
3. Prefer live patterns in [component-library.html](../../component-library.html) and existing JSX over inventing new CSS.

## Tokens

- Use semantic CSS variables from [assets/global.css](../../assets/global.css) — never primitive palette hex values directly.
- Examples: `var(--background)`, `var(--foreground)`, `var(--primary)`, `var(--muted-foreground)`, `var(--accent-green)`, `var(--border)`.
- Themes: `data-theme="light"` (default), `"dark"`, `"jurnii-v1"`.
- On light surfaces use `--accent-green` (not `jurnii-200`) for solid green fills.

## Typography & layout

- Font: Geist (`--font-sans`), Geist Mono (`--font-mono`).
- Marketing headings: `.h1-page`, `.h2-section`, `h1.display` — see website design system.
- Helpers: `.eyebrow`, `.lede`, `.section-lede`, `.body-md`.
- Layout: `.container`, `.section`, `.section-tight`; spacing/radius via `--spacing-*` / `--radius-*`.

## Components (reuse first)

- Shell: `PageChrome` from [assets/site.jsx](../../assets/site.jsx).
- Blocks: `PageHero`, `FeatureGrid`, `OutcomeStrip`, `Methodology`, `Testimonials`, `PersonaList`, `CTABand` from [assets/blocks.jsx](../../assets/blocks.jsx).
- Buttons: `.btn.primary`, `.btn.ghost`, `.btn.accent` with optional `.lg`.
- Icons: Lucide via `<i data-lucide="name" />` — call `lucide.createIcons()` after render.

## Babel / React conventions

- Export shared components: `window.MyComponent = MyComponent`.
- Never name a style object `styles` — use scoped names (`heroStyles`) or inline styles.
- Poll for required globals before `ReactDOM.createRoot(...).render(...)`.
- Keep "Book a demo" → `contact-us.html` so the demo modal fires.

## Motion & voice

- Add `.reveal` to sections; register new card grids / stats in `FX_STAGGER_GROUPS` / `FX_COUNT_TARGETS` in `site.jsx`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- No emoji. Sharp, evidence-led copy for iGaming operators.

## Do not

- Hardcode colours, fonts, or spacing that exist as CSS variables.
- Create one-off components when an existing block or `component-library.html` pattern covers it.
- Reference primitive tokens (`--concrete-*`, `--jurnii-*`) in component CSS — use semantic aliases.
- Duplicate token tables across docs — brand doc owns tokens; website doc owns implementation.
